   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to the establishment of a home visitation program for elderly and invalid victims of violent crime",
    "basePrintNo": "S4909",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4909-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 20,
       "fullName": "Jesse Hamilton",
       "imgName": "889_jesse_hamilton.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 889,
       "sessionMemberId": 937,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "HAMILTON"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §623, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4909\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to the establishment of\na home visitation program for elderly and invalid victims of violent\ncrime\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo create a volunteer program of home visitation to elderly and\ninvalid victims of violent crime, in consultation with the NYS Office\nfor the Aging.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends the Executive Law, section 623, subdivision 9.\nProvides that the New York State Office for the Aging shall be\nconsulted in order to promote the establishment of a volunteer program\nof home visitation to elderly and invalid victims of violent crime.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date.\n\n CURRENT LAW :\n\nCurrent statute provides for a special investigative unit to expedite\nand process claims for elderly and invalid victims of violent crime\nand to promote the establishment of a volunteer home visitation\nprogram for such victims. This bill would require the State Office for\nthe Aging to be consulted in cases involving the home visitation\nprogram.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill would enable the State Office for the Aging to be consulted\nin the establishment and maintenance of a special investigative unit\nthat expedites claims of senior citizens and special emergency\nsituations involving elderly and invalid victims of violent crimes.\nThis unit also would be charged with the establishment of a volunteer\nhome visitation program for these victims.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016: S.267 - REFERRED TO CRIME VICTIMS, CRIME AND CORRECTION/A.300 -\npassed assembly\n2015: S.267 - REFERRED TO CRIME VICTIMS, CRIME AND CORRECTION/A.300 -\npassed assembly\n2014: S.313 - Referred to Crime Victims, Crime and Correction/A.449 -\nPassed Assembly\n2013: S.313 - Reported and Committed to Rules/A.449 Passed Assembly\n2012: S.3559- Notice of Committee Consideration Requested, Defeated in\nCrime Victims, Crime and Correction/ A.5439 - Passed Assembly\n2011: S.3559- Notice of Committee Consideration Requested/A.5439 -\nPassed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately\n",
